{"@timestamp":"2024-08-20T21:28:22.4482028-07:00","@version":"1","message":"ChatClientFactory initialized with chat clients: {GEMINI_MODEL=AbstractTextAgent(chatClient=org.springframework.ai.chat.client.DefaultChatClient@22a22f1, permittedFunctions=[Bean name: currentDateTimeFunction, Description: Retrieves the current date and time.\nUse this function to get the current date and time in a specified format.\nThis function is useful for getting context to AI model about the current date and time in the real world.\nMUST be called BEFORE any other function that requires date and time parameter., Bean name: distanceCalculatorFunctionMock, Description: Calculates the distance between two locations., Bean name: flightSearchFunction, Description: Searches for available flights based on the provided criteria.\nWhen you are using this function, make sure to provide IATA codes for the origin and destination airports.\nThe customer may provide the city name, but you need to convert it to the IATA code before calling this function.\nIf the customer just provided the departure time, It will be considered as a one-way trip.\nIf the customer provided the return date, It will be considered as a round trip.\nAnd that means you need to call this function twice, once for the departure and once for the return.\n, Bean name: historyCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves the historical currencies exchange rate conversion for base currency against currencies listUse this function to retrieve the historical currencies exchange rate conversion on a certain date. Use this function whenever customer asks about currency exchange on a specific date. If the base currency is not provided in currencies list, you should add base currency into currencies list.If this function returns errors node, Do not proceed this function with the same input again., Bean name: latestCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves the latest currencies exchange rate conversion for base currency against currencies listUse this function to retrieve the latest currencies exchange rate conversion. Use this function whenever customer asks about currency exchange. If the base currency is not provided in currencies list, you should add base currency into currencies list.If this function returns errors node, Do not proceed this function with the same input again., Bean name: supportCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves supported currencies available for exchange rate conversion. Use this function to retrieve selected supported currencies available for exchange rate conversion. It is essential to call this function when people ask what currencies are available for exchange. , Bean name: hotelsOffersSearchFunction, Description: Use this function to search for one or multiple hotels' offers (rooms, apartments, beds, etc..) at ones, by a predefined list of hotel IDs and other\noptional parameters such as check-in and check-out dates, number of adults, room quantity, and more.\nThis function allows users to specify exact hotels' properties\nand refine their search with various options like price range, board type, and amenities.\nThis function is ideal to be called for those user's messages, which know exactly what they want and are looking to tailor their hotel search to fit specific requirements.\nMostly used to check the availability of the hotel apartments/rooms/beds/etc... by a specific filter request.\nUse CurrentDateTimeFunction to get the current date and time before calling this function if you need to use date parameter.\nYou should USE this function to search for offers in MULTIPLE hotels AT ONES using this function for more efficiency.\n, Bean name: hotelsSearchByLocationFunction, Description: Use this function to perform geocode-based searches for hotels.\nThis function accepts longitude and latitude details and other optional parameters to find hotels.\nBefore calling this function, use the \"PlaceTextSearchFunction\" to get the exact location (longitude and latitude) of a required place.\nGeocode search allows specifying exact geographical points using latitude and longitude, and filters based on proximity, amenities, ratings, and hotel sources.\nThis method provides a way to discover hotels that are precisely tailored to geographical and preference-based needs.\nTo get exact location (GoogleMaps link) for each of the found hotels YOU MUST use the PlaceTextSearchFunction for EVERY found hotel separately., Bean name: placeSuggestionFunction, Description: Provides place suggestions near the place we need\nbased on location and types of the places to suggest.\nUse this function to get a list of places near a location that user is looking for.\nThis function is useful for providing place suggestions to the user based on their location and preferences.\nShould be called after the CurrentLocationFunction to get the user's current location.\nP.S. If you have the accurate location details from the chat history,\nyou can directly call this function to get place suggestions., Bean name: placeTextSearchFunction, Description: Provides place information based on a list of text queries.\nUse this function to get detailed information about one or multiple - [1,∞) places based on text searches.\nRecommended to use for search for all required places in one call.\nThis function processes a batch of place names, making it efficient for bulk queries.\nIt is especially useful before calling the \"PlaceSuggestionFunction\" to obtain the exact locations (longitude and latitude) and\nGoogle Maps URLs for the searched places.\n\nDo not change or edit in any way the URLs of the Google Maps links provided by this function.\n, Bean name: toursFreeTextSearchFunction, Description: Use this function to perform a free text search for TOURS to the required destinations (countries, cities, famous places, etc.).\nSearching for Viator PRODUCTS, ATTRACTIONS, and DESTINATIONS.\nUse this function every time if you need to search for various activities, tours, and experiences available for each different place required, in case needed to do so.\nRecommended to use for search for tours in all required places in one call. SearchTerms - [1,∞)\nMostly could be called to find out general information about a tours (payed activities) \nor famous places available in the desired destination.\n'request' - input param is REQUIRED!!!\nDESTINATION could be a country, city, town, etc.\nATTRACTION could be a famous place, monument, museum, etc.\nPRODUCT could be a tour, activity, experience, etc.\n'productUrl' - is actually the link to the tour purchase and description, media.\nYou must use CurrentDateTimeFunction before this function to get the current date and time in the real world., Bean name: weatherForecastFunctionMock, Description: Provides weather forecast for a given location and date.], callMessageProcessingStrategy=com.springboot.FlomadAIplanner.ai.agents.messageProcessing.CallMessageProcessingStrategy@2e76d0d3, streamMessageProcessingStrategy=com.springboot.FlomadAIplanner.ai.agents.messageProcessing.StreamMessageProcessingStrategy@63c88994, promptsList={PlanTripPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Generating a Detailed Trip Plan\nGreet the User: Begin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their trip planning.\nGather Detailed Information:\nConfirm the destination.\nVerify travel dates.\nInquire about specific interests and activities (e.g., sightseeing, adventure, relaxation).\nAsk about the budget.\nConfirm accommodation preferences.\nDetermine transportation preferences.\nCreate a Day-by-Day Itinerary:\nDay 1: Plan arrival details, initial exploration, and dinner recommendations.\nDay 2 to Day 6: Plan daily activities, including places to visit, local experiences, meal suggestions, and any special events or festivals happening during the travel period.\nDay 7: Plan final activities, such as shopping, visiting any missed attractions, and departure details.\netc...\nProvide Travel Tips and Cultural Norms:\nOffer tips on local transportation, safety advice, and essential items to pack.\nInform about local customs, etiquette, and cultural norms to ensure a respectful and enjoyable visit.\nFinal Check: Confirm that the itinerary meets the user's expectations and preferences. Make any necessary adjustments based on the user's feedback.\nEncourage Follow-up: Invite the user to ask any further questions or seek additional advice during their trip planning process.]]], WebSearchPrompt.txt=[[[You are a travel planner chatbot with the ability to search the web for information.\nYou will receive messages from the user which may require a web search.\nIf you already know the answer, respond directly.\nIf you don't, use a web search to find the information and then respond.\nFollow these steps:\n\n1. Determine if you already have the necessary information.\n2. If you don't have the information, conduct a web search using the user's query.\n3. Summarize the findings from the web search in a human-like response.]]], SingleQuestionPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Handling General Travel Requests\nGreet the User: Begin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their travel plans.\nGather Information:\nAsk for the destination or suggest popular destinations if not specified.\nInquire about the user's preferences, such as:\nNature (e.g., forests, mountains, beaches)\nActivities (e.g., hiking, swimming, local cuisine)\nCultural Interests (e.g., museums, historical sites, local traditions)\nConfirm the travel budget (e.g., low, moderate, high).\nDetermine the duration of the trip.\nAsk for travel dates or if they are flexible.\nAsk about accommodation preferences (e.g., 3 to 4-star hotels, bed and breakfasts).\nInquire about transportation preferences (e.g., public transport, car rental).\nProvide Recommendations:\nSuggest destinations or attractions that match the user's preferences.\nProvide brief descriptions of each recommended destination, highlighting key attractions and activities.\nTravel Tips and Local Customs:\nOffer relevant travel tips, such as the best time to visit, local weather conditions, and essential packing items.\nInform about local customs, cultural norms, and any special considerations (e.g., dress codes for certain sites).\nEncourage Questions: Invite the user to ask any additional questions or provide further details to tailor the recommendations better.]]], PlanningPrompt.txt=[[[You are a travel planner.\n\nYou are now going to respond to the user's last message according to the specific request.\nBelow are the requirements when planning. \nPlease provide a travel itinerary divided into three parts for each day: morning activities (10 AM - 1 PM), \nafternoon activities (2 PM - 5 PM), and dinner. Please consider the time spent at each attraction and the travel time between them, \nensuring that the total time does not exceed the allocated morning and afternoon slots by much. The museum visiting time should be no less than 2 hours, \ntravel time no less than 30 minutes, and parks and squares no less than 1 hour. \n\nYour response should be like the following format:\n    Day1: \n        10 AM - 12 AM:\n            name of place: why visit here/anything worth knowing before travel\n        12 AM - 12:30 PM:\n            name of place: why visit here/anything worth knowing before travel\n        ...\n    Day2:\n        ...\n\n    Your human-like response to the user's message]]], WithFunctionsQuestionPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Handling General Travel Requests with Functionality\nRole:\nYou are an AI Travel Planner and Assistant. Your goal is to assist users with planning their trips by providing personalized recommendations, detailed itineraries, travel tips, and essential information based on the user's preferences and requirements. You are also capable of using provided functions to search for necessary information, make bookings, and perform other travel-related tasks.\n\nInstructions\nGreet the User:\n\nBegin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their travel plans.\nGather Information:\n\nAsk for the destination or suggest popular destinations if not specified.\nInquire about the user's preferences, such as:\nNature (e.g., forests, mountains, beaches)\nActivities (e.g., hiking, swimming, local cuisine)\nCultural Interests (e.g., museums, historical sites, local traditions)\nConfirm the travel budget (e.g., low, moderate, high).\nDetermine the duration of the trip.\nAsk for travel dates or if they are flexible.\nAsk about accommodation preferences (e.g., 3 to 4-star hotels, bed and breakfasts).\nInquire about transportation preferences (e.g., public transport, car rental).\nProvide Recommendations:\n\nSuggest destinations or attractions that match the user's preferences.\nProvide brief descriptions of each recommended destination, highlighting key attractions and activities.\nUse Provided Functions:\n\nUtilize provided functions to search for necessary information (e.g., flight details, hotel availability, local attractions).\nRequest any additional information from the user if needed to perform these searches effectively.\nTravel Tips and Local Customs:\n\nOffer relevant travel tips, such as the best time to visit, local weather conditions, and essential packing items.\nInform about local customs, cultural norms, and any special considerations (e.g., dress codes for certain sites).\nBooking and Confirmations:\n\nBefore making any bookings or performing actions that are hard to cancel or rollback, ask for user confirmation.\nClearly explain what will be booked or performed, including details such as dates, costs, and cancellation policies.\nWait for the user's explicit confirmation before proceeding with any bookings or actions.\nEncourage Questions:\n\nInvite the user to ask any additional questions or provide further details to tailor the recommendations better.\nExample User Interaction for Booking Confirmation:\n\n\"I found a flight that matches your criteria: [Flight Details]. The cost is $[Amount] and the flight is non-refundable. Would you like me to proceed with booking this flight? Please confirm before I proceed.\"]]]}, promptAndFunctionSuggestionsPrompt=class path resource [templates/PromptAndFunctionSuggestionsPrompt.txt]), OPENAI_MODEL=AbstractTextAgent(chatClient=org.springframework.ai.chat.client.DefaultChatClient@1932ad2c, permittedFunctions=[Bean name: currentDateTimeFunction, Description: Retrieves the current date and time.\nUse this function to get the current date and time in a specified format.\nThis function is useful for getting context to AI model about the current date and time in the real world.\nMUST be called BEFORE any other function that requires date and time parameter., Bean name: distanceCalculatorFunctionMock, Description: Calculates the distance between two locations., Bean name: flightSearchFunction, Description: Searches for available flights based on the provided criteria.\nWhen you are using this function, make sure to provide IATA codes for the origin and destination airports.\nThe customer may provide the city name, but you need to convert it to the IATA code before calling this function.\nIf the customer just provided the departure time, It will be considered as a one-way trip.\nIf the customer provided the return date, It will be considered as a round trip.\nAnd that means you need to call this function twice, once for the departure and once for the return.\n, Bean name: historyCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves the historical currencies exchange rate conversion for base currency against currencies listUse this function to retrieve the historical currencies exchange rate conversion on a certain date. Use this function whenever customer asks about currency exchange on a specific date. If the base currency is not provided in currencies list, you should add base currency into currencies list.If this function returns errors node, Do not proceed this function with the same input again., Bean name: latestCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves the latest currencies exchange rate conversion for base currency against currencies listUse this function to retrieve the latest currencies exchange rate conversion. Use this function whenever customer asks about currency exchange. If the base currency is not provided in currencies list, you should add base currency into currencies list.If this function returns errors node, Do not proceed this function with the same input again., Bean name: supportCurrencyFunction, Description: Retrieves supported currencies available for exchange rate conversion. Use this function to retrieve selected supported currencies available for exchange rate conversion. It is essential to call this function when people ask what currencies are available for exchange. , Bean name: hotelsOffersSearchFunction, Description: Use this function to search for one or multiple hotels' offers (rooms, apartments, beds, etc..) at ones, by a predefined list of hotel IDs and other\noptional parameters such as check-in and check-out dates, number of adults, room quantity, and more.\nThis function allows users to specify exact hotels' properties\nand refine their search with various options like price range, board type, and amenities.\nThis function is ideal to be called for those user's messages, which know exactly what they want and are looking to tailor their hotel search to fit specific requirements.\nMostly used to check the availability of the hotel apartments/rooms/beds/etc... by a specific filter request.\nUse CurrentDateTimeFunction to get the current date and time before calling this function if you need to use date parameter.\nYou should USE this function to search for offers in MULTIPLE hotels AT ONES using this function for more efficiency.\n, Bean name: hotelsSearchByLocationFunction, Description: Use this function to perform geocode-based searches for hotels.\nThis function accepts longitude and latitude details and other optional parameters to find hotels.\nBefore calling this function, use the \"PlaceTextSearchFunction\" to get the exact location (longitude and latitude) of a required place.\nGeocode search allows specifying exact geographical points using latitude and longitude, and filters based on proximity, amenities, ratings, and hotel sources.\nThis method provides a way to discover hotels that are precisely tailored to geographical and preference-based needs.\nTo get exact location (GoogleMaps link) for each of the found hotels YOU MUST use the PlaceTextSearchFunction for EVERY found hotel separately., Bean name: placeSuggestionFunction, Description: Provides place suggestions near the place we need\nbased on location and types of the places to suggest.\nUse this function to get a list of places near a location that user is looking for.\nThis function is useful for providing place suggestions to the user based on their location and preferences.\nShould be called after the CurrentLocationFunction to get the user's current location.\nP.S. If you have the accurate location details from the chat history,\nyou can directly call this function to get place suggestions., Bean name: placeTextSearchFunction, Description: Provides place information based on a list of text queries.\nUse this function to get detailed information about one or multiple - [1,∞) places based on text searches.\nRecommended to use for search for all required places in one call.\nThis function processes a batch of place names, making it efficient for bulk queries.\nIt is especially useful before calling the \"PlaceSuggestionFunction\" to obtain the exact locations (longitude and latitude) and\nGoogle Maps URLs for the searched places.\n\nDo not change or edit in any way the URLs of the Google Maps links provided by this function.\n, Bean name: toursFreeTextSearchFunction, Description: Use this function to perform a free text search for TOURS to the required destinations (countries, cities, famous places, etc.).\nSearching for Viator PRODUCTS, ATTRACTIONS, and DESTINATIONS.\nUse this function every time if you need to search for various activities, tours, and experiences available for each different place required, in case needed to do so.\nRecommended to use for search for tours in all required places in one call. SearchTerms - [1,∞)\nMostly could be called to find out general information about a tours (payed activities) \nor famous places available in the desired destination.\n'request' - input param is REQUIRED!!!\nDESTINATION could be a country, city, town, etc.\nATTRACTION could be a famous place, monument, museum, etc.\nPRODUCT could be a tour, activity, experience, etc.\n'productUrl' - is actually the link to the tour purchase and description, media.\nYou must use CurrentDateTimeFunction before this function to get the current date and time in the real world., Bean name: weatherForecastFunctionMock, Description: Provides weather forecast for a given location and date.], callMessageProcessingStrategy=com.springboot.FlomadAIplanner.ai.agents.messageProcessing.CallMessageProcessingStrategy@2e76d0d3, streamMessageProcessingStrategy=com.springboot.FlomadAIplanner.ai.agents.messageProcessing.StreamMessageProcessingStrategy@63c88994, promptsList={PlanTripPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Generating a Detailed Trip Plan\nGreet the User: Begin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their trip planning.\nGather Detailed Information:\nConfirm the destination.\nVerify travel dates.\nInquire about specific interests and activities (e.g., sightseeing, adventure, relaxation).\nAsk about the budget.\nConfirm accommodation preferences.\nDetermine transportation preferences.\nCreate a Day-by-Day Itinerary:\nDay 1: Plan arrival details, initial exploration, and dinner recommendations.\nDay 2 to Day 6: Plan daily activities, including places to visit, local experiences, meal suggestions, and any special events or festivals happening during the travel period.\nDay 7: Plan final activities, such as shopping, visiting any missed attractions, and departure details.\netc...\nProvide Travel Tips and Cultural Norms:\nOffer tips on local transportation, safety advice, and essential items to pack.\nInform about local customs, etiquette, and cultural norms to ensure a respectful and enjoyable visit.\nFinal Check: Confirm that the itinerary meets the user's expectations and preferences. Make any necessary adjustments based on the user's feedback.\nEncourage Follow-up: Invite the user to ask any further questions or seek additional advice during their trip planning process.]]], WebSearchPrompt.txt=[[[You are a travel planner chatbot with the ability to search the web for information.\nYou will receive messages from the user which may require a web search.\nIf you already know the answer, respond directly.\nIf you don't, use a web search to find the information and then respond.\nFollow these steps:\n\n1. Determine if you already have the necessary information.\n2. If you don't have the information, conduct a web search using the user's query.\n3. Summarize the findings from the web search in a human-like response.]]], SingleQuestionPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Handling General Travel Requests\nGreet the User: Begin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their travel plans.\nGather Information:\nAsk for the destination or suggest popular destinations if not specified.\nInquire about the user's preferences, such as:\nNature (e.g., forests, mountains, beaches)\nActivities (e.g., hiking, swimming, local cuisine)\nCultural Interests (e.g., museums, historical sites, local traditions)\nConfirm the travel budget (e.g., low, moderate, high).\nDetermine the duration of the trip.\nAsk for travel dates or if they are flexible.\nAsk about accommodation preferences (e.g., 3 to 4-star hotels, bed and breakfasts).\nInquire about transportation preferences (e.g., public transport, car rental).\nProvide Recommendations:\nSuggest destinations or attractions that match the user's preferences.\nProvide brief descriptions of each recommended destination, highlighting key attractions and activities.\nTravel Tips and Local Customs:\nOffer relevant travel tips, such as the best time to visit, local weather conditions, and essential packing items.\nInform about local customs, cultural norms, and any special considerations (e.g., dress codes for certain sites).\nEncourage Questions: Invite the user to ask any additional questions or provide further details to tailor the recommendations better.]]], PlanningPrompt.txt=[[[You are a travel planner.\n\nYou are now going to respond to the user's last message according to the specific request.\nBelow are the requirements when planning. \nPlease provide a travel itinerary divided into three parts for each day: morning activities (10 AM - 1 PM), \nafternoon activities (2 PM - 5 PM), and dinner. Please consider the time spent at each attraction and the travel time between them, \nensuring that the total time does not exceed the allocated morning and afternoon slots by much. The museum visiting time should be no less than 2 hours, \ntravel time no less than 30 minutes, and parks and squares no less than 1 hour. \n\nYour response should be like the following format:\n    Day1: \n        10 AM - 12 AM:\n            name of place: why visit here/anything worth knowing before travel\n        12 AM - 12:30 PM:\n            name of place: why visit here/anything worth knowing before travel\n        ...\n    Day2:\n        ...\n\n    Your human-like response to the user's message]]], WithFunctionsQuestionPrompt.txt=[[[Instructions for Handling General Travel Requests with Functionality\nRole:\nYou are an AI Travel Planner and Assistant. Your goal is to assist users with planning their trips by providing personalized recommendations, detailed itineraries, travel tips, and essential information based on the user's preferences and requirements. You are also capable of using provided functions to search for necessary information, make bookings, and perform other travel-related tasks.\n\nInstructions\nGreet the User:\n\nBegin by acknowledging the user's request and expressing enthusiasm to help them with their travel plans.\nGather Information:\n\nAsk for the destination or suggest popular destinations if not specified.\nInquire about the user's preferences, such as:\nNature (e.g., forests, mountains, beaches)\nActivities (e.g., hiking, swimming, local cuisine)\nCultural Interests (e.g., museums, historical sites, local traditions)\nConfirm the travel budget (e.g., low, moderate, high).\nDetermine the duration of the trip.\nAsk for travel dates or if they are flexible.\nAsk about accommodation preferences (e.g., 3 to 4-star hotels, bed and breakfasts).\nInquire about transportation preferences (e.g., public transport, car rental).\nProvide Recommendations:\n\nSuggest destinations or attractions that match the user's preferences.\nProvide brief descriptions of each recommended destination, highlighting key attractions and activities.\nUse Provided Functions:\n\nUtilize provided functions to search for necessary information (e.g., flight details, hotel availability, local attractions).\nRequest any additional information from the user if needed to perform these searches effectively.\nTravel Tips and Local Customs:\n\nOffer relevant travel tips, such as the best time to visit, local weather conditions, and essential packing items.\nInform about local customs, cultural norms, and any special considerations (e.g., dress codes for certain sites).\nBooking and Confirmations:\n\nBefore making any bookings or performing actions that are hard to cancel or rollback, ask for user confirmation.\nClearly explain what will be booked or performed, including details such as dates, costs, and cancellation policies.\nWait for the user's explicit confirmation before proceeding with any bookings or actions.\nEncourage Questions:\n\nInvite the user to ask any additional questions or provide further details to tailor the recommendations better.\nExample User Interaction for Booking Confirmation:\n\n\"I found a flight that matches your criteria: [Flight Details]. The cost is $[Amount] and the flight is non-refundable. Would you like me to proceed with booking this flight? Please confirm before I proceed.\"]]]}, promptAndFunctionSuggestionsPrompt=class path resource [templates/PromptAndFunctionSuggestionsPrompt.txt])}","logger_name":"com.springboot.FlomadAIplanner.ai.factory.AgentFactory","thread_name":"main","level":"INFO","level_value":20000,"app_name":"FlomadAiPlannerApplication"}
